      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The escrow agent has significant legal and fiduciary responsibilities, which means they are legally bound to act solely in the best interest of the transaction, not their own. They are subject to strict regulations and oversight, which is why they are licensed professionals. If they were to mismanage the funds or act improperly, they face severe legal consequences, which is a major deterrent. Think of it as a highly regulated system designed to prevent exactly the kind of shady dealings you're worried about.",
